2. Data, designs and interoperability facts from other projects
===============================================================

No source code of the projects below was copied into spoor. Where spoor
reuses their data (identifiers, paths, names, lists) or reimplements one of
their algorithms so that results interoperate, the project is credited here
and next to the code that uses it. All reused data was re-checked against
primary sources while spoor was built and was changed where it was found to
be wrong or too broad; the files named below are modified works in that
sense. "Read" dates are when the source was consulted.

uber/ADR (ADR: Agentic AI Detection and Response)
  https://github.com/uber/adr, commit 6b33dff (2026-10-16), read 2026-11-11
  Copyright 2024 ADR Project Contributors. Licensed under the Apache
  License, Version 2.0.
  - Agent catalogue facts: product ids, binary and package names, bundle,
    desktop and extension identifiers and install paths in
    internal/catalog/data/*.yaml were cross-checked with, and partly derive
    from, ADR Discovery's catalog.json (catalog version 2026.10.12). The
    GitHub Actions references of CI agents come from ADR Discovery's
    workflow extractor (Discovery/adr_discovery/extractor/formats/
    workflow.py).
  - Skill folder hash: internal/discovery/skillhash.go reimplements ADR
    Discovery's skill folder hash so that its result is byte-compatible and
    skill indicators interoperate.
  - Model-provider host suffixes (Discovery/adr_discovery/enumerator/
    markers.py) in internal/classify/hostdata.go.
  - Claude Code session-log record types that carry no activity
    (_METADATA_RECORD_TYPES of ADR Sensor's claude_parser.py) and the record
    shapes that parser reads, cross-checked in internal/transcript/claude.go.
  - The value-taking-flag approach to reading an MCP server launch line
    (Discovery judge/risk.py) in internal/mcpconf; plugin registry field
    names read the same way as ADR's reader in internal/discovery/plugins.go.
  - Test method: negative controls and per-run canary credentials searched
    for in the output, as in ADR Discovery's test harness
    (internal/discovery tests).
  Nothing from ADR Detection, ADR-Bench or the third-party material listed
  in ADR's NOTICE.md is included.

